  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "like + -ing: affirmative (I like reading) and questions (Do you like ...?)",
      "title_form": "Like + -ing: afirmativo y preguntas",
      "title_target": "Like + -ing: affirmative and questions",
      "description_md_form": "Para hablar de **gustos** en inglés, usamos el verbo **like** (gustar) seguido de un verbo con **-ing**. Por ejemplo: **I like reading** (Me gusta leer).\n\nPara preguntar sobre gustos, usamos **Do you like...?** (¿Te gusta...?). La respuesta corta es **Yes, I do** o **No, I don't**.\n\n**Estructura:**\n- Afirmativo: **I like + verbo-ing**\n- Pregunta: **Do you like + verbo-ing?**\n\nEjemplos:\n- **I like reading books.** (Me gusta leer libros.)\n- **Do you like music?** (¿Te gusta la música?)\n\nEste patrón es muy común para hablar de hobbies y preferencias.",
      "description_md_target": "To talk about **likes** in English, we use the verb **like** followed by a verb with **-ing**. For example: **I like reading**.\n\nTo ask about likes, we use **Do you like...?** The short answer is **Yes, I do** or **No, I don't**.\n\n**Structure:**\n- Affirmative: **I like + verb-ing**\n- Question: **Do you like + verb-ing?**\n\nExamples:\n- **I like reading books.**\n- **Do you like music?**\n\nThis pattern is very common for talking about hobbies and preferences.",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject + like + verb-ing / Do + subject + like + verb-ing?",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "like + -ing",
        "headers": [
          "Forma",
          "Ejemplo"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Afirmativo",
            "I like reading."
          ],
          [
            "Pregunta",
            "Do you like reading?"
          ],
          [
            "Respuesta corta sí",
            "Yes, I do."
          ],
          [
            "Respuesta corta no",
            "No, I don't."
          ]
        ]
      },
      "examples": [
